        <title type="html"><![CDATA[FF152 TC39 Iterator includes]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29746</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29746"/>
        <updated>2026-06-01T12:14:47.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF152 adds support for the <a href="https://github.com/tc39/proposal-iterator-includes">TC39 Iterator proposal</a> in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2025779" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2025779</a> behind pref <code class="notranslate">javascript.options.experimental.iterator_includes</code></p>
<p dir="auto">This adds the feature for the <code class="notranslate">Iterator.includes()</code> builtin.<br>
Note, I can't see evidence it is supported yet by anyone other than FF, which seems reasonable given it is early in the cycle.</p>
<p dir="auto">It fails because of the spec url which is the github repo.<br>
I tried <a href="https://tc39.es/proposal-iterator-includes/" rel="nofollow">https://tc39.es/proposal-iterator-includes/</a> as well but that didn't work.<br>
I'm after advice, since it looks in the browser spec repo that tc39 specs are allowed ....</p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4469264809" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44158" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/44158/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44158">mdn/content#44158</a></p>]]></content>
